# TAP groups exercised by CI-tier-sweep (the merge-only v3.0/v3.1 sweep).
#
#   a group is listed IFF it is
#     (1) already wired into regular CI (a CI-<group>.yml caller, the name
#         appears in a workflow on this branch or on origin/GH-Actions, or it
#         is in a dynamically discovered family) -- the same definition as
#         test/tap/groups/lint_group_coverage.py; AND
#     (2) not in a family the sweep's stock build cannot run (see below); AND
#     (3) selectable on at least one of v3.0 / v3.1.
#
# Condition (2) exists because (1) is necessary but NOT sufficient. The six
# cluster_sim_* groups are wired -- CI-cluster-simulator.yml discovers them at
# run time -- but that workflow also runs `make build_cluster_simulator` and
# stages test/deps/cluster_simulator, and the group env files point at that
# binary. The sweep builds a stock `make ubuntu24-tap` handoff which does not
# contain it, and run-tests-isolated.bash has no simulator handling, so these
# groups would fail every run for a reason unrelated to the tier. They are
# excluded deliberately. Teaching the sweep to build and stage the simulator is
# the work that would let them back in.
#
ai-g1
ai-g2
legacy-binlog-g1
